1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,860
These three mistakes

2
00:00:00,860 --> 00:00:03,360
make your edits look like an amateur.

3
00:00:03,440 --> 00:00:04,220
Here's what you should do

4
00:00:04,220 --> 00:00:05,040
to take your animation

5
00:00:05,040 --> 00:00:06,950
from beginner to professional.

6
00:00:06,960 --> 00:00:08,800
Number 1: Stop oversizing everything

7
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:15,040
As a rule of thumb,

8
00:00:15,040 --> 00:00:16,950
the next time you're creating an animation,

9
00:00:16,980 --> 00:00:19,040
make every element 25% smaller

10
00:00:19,040 --> 00:00:21,240
and just watch how much better it looks.

11
00:00:21,340 --> 00:00:23,080
Number 2: Stop overusing effects

12
00:00:23,100 --> 00:00:24,780
Less is more.

13
00:00:24,780 --> 00:00:26,300
The less you use an effect,

14
00:00:26,300 --> 00:00:27,920
the more special it is.

15
00:00:32,140 --> 00:00:34,160
Number 3: Use more dull colors

16
00:00:34,180 --> 00:00:35,860
Beginner editors always use

17
00:00:35,860 --> 00:00:37,420
harsh blacks, harsh whites,

18
00:00:37,420 --> 00:00:38,900
and bright reds.

19
00:00:45,820 --> 00:00:47,080
So now that you know that,

20
00:00:47,080 --> 00:00:48,880
change these three things about your edits

21
00:00:48,880 --> 00:00:50,320
and watch your animations go

22
00:00:50,320 --> 00:00:51,820
from beginner to professional.
